<http://data.silknow.org/event/b2401554-5a6d-3956-ae6e-1ac8cdfafc3f>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "All the figures in the medallions are copied from prints showing recently discovered Roman wall-paintings, from the nine volume work <i>Le Antichità di Ercolano</i> (1757-1792). The two larger medallions below the pockets show The Cupid Seller, discovered at the Villa Arianna in Stabiae, a subject much copied after its publication in 1762. Other images are drawn from wall paintings found at Cicero's Villa in Pompeii. \nThe waistcoat was formerly in the Robinson Collection."@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/e2048707-f02b-36c6-b4aa-8b41723eed15> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "All the figures in the medallions are copied from prints showing recently discovered Roman wall-paintings, from the nine volume work <i>Le Antichità di Ercolano</i> (1757-1792). The two larger medallions below the pockets show The Cupid Seller, discovered at the Villa Arianna in Stabiae, a subject much copied after its publication in 1762. Other images are drawn from wall paintings found at Cicero's Villa in Pompeii. \nThe waistcoat was formerly in the Robinson Collection."@en .

