<http://data.silknow.org/object/e2048707-f02b-36c6-b4aa-8b41723eed15/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The influence of Neo-classical design is evident in the decoration of this waistcoat of the 1780s. Embroidered floral garlands and ribbons, elements of late-18th century decoration, adorn the pockets. Medallions of twill silk minutely and skilfully painted in black with mythological classical figures have been applied to the front and collar. The square-cut shape, standing collar and welt pocket are characteristic of the waistcoat styles in the 1780s."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/e2048707-f02b-36c6-b4aa-8b41723eed15> .

